            <div xml:id="d91">

                <pb facs="0091" n="83" sameAs="frus:frus1937v04/pg83"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94 Conference/41: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Grew</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-10-18T10:00:00+09:00">October 18, 1937—10
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received October 17—11:45 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>479. Embassy’s 476 [<hi rendition="#italic">475</hi>], October 15, 5 p.m.,
                    paragraph 2, Nine Power Treaty Conference. It may be well to record that one of
                    the arguments which I used in my conversation with Hirota was that the proposed
                    Conference would offer Japan a forum to present the views for which purpose it
                    is sending so-called good will envoys to America and Europe.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
